  "explains": "The constant Paths.STATUS changes from BASE + /status to BASE + /state. Paths has two importers by use: StatusController, in the same package (no import line), spells Paths.STATUS twice, in the mapping of status and in the mapping of flags (Paths.STATUS + /flags); InvoiceController spells Paths.INVOICES only and is excluded by narrowing. So the two routes whose path the constant is part of are reached: GET /ledger/v1/state and GET /ledger/v1/state/flags, and the evidence of each cites the line of the constant that gives the path. The old routes GET /ledger/v1/status and GET /ledger/v1/status/flags are gone. The web client still names /ledger/v1/status (STATUS_URL, fetchStatus): the removed route is still called, which is a finding with high risk and low confidence, and after the change the URL fits no route, so the edge says the call matched nothing (client_url_unmatched, and a blocking edge_incomplete: an added route cannot be called uncalled while a call fits nothing). The client call is followed to the screen /status. Nothing calls /status/flags.",
  "complete_for": [
    "changed_symbol",
    "caller",
    "route",
    "screen",
    "http_edge",
    "finding"
  ],
